      <h1>How to Set Up a Bitcoin Development Environment</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">A Bitcoin development environment should separate source code, build output, test data, credentials, and real funds. The right setup depends on whether the goal is to call a released node, study implementation code, build Bitcoin Core, write tests, or operate an application. Current Bitcoin Core uses CMake, and safe local experiments normally belong on regtest with dedicated wallets and data directories rather than mainnet.</p>
      <ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Infrastructure</li><li>Deep</li><li>Technical Explainer</li><li>21 to 24 minutes</li><li>Reviewed 2026-07-26</li></ul>
